20260517182247 Difference you observed: - `Kardenwort Sub Viewer` likely had a different icon because Windows resolved a different target/icon source for that `.lnk` (or cached icon metadata already existed). - Your first `FFmpeg Convert Media` attempt did not create the shortcut in the real profile folder, so Explorer had nothing to show immediately. - Once created correctly, Explorer sometimes shows it immediately, sometimes after refresh/sign-out due to Explorer icon/menu cache timing. What I changed in [convert_media.py](u:\voothi\20241213164711-convert-media\convert_media.py): - Refactored and moved hardcoded values to a clear top config block. - Added explicit configurable output behavior: - `--output-mode same-dir|converted-subdir` (default now `same-dir`) - `--duplicate-mode zid-dir|skip|overwrite` (default `zid-dir`) - `--converted-subdir-name ` (used only with `converted-subdir`) - Kept ZID duplicate handling, now relative to selected output mode: - With `same-dir`, duplicate goes to `\\.mp4` - Kept backward compatibility for legacy direct conversion mode. - Improved shortcut creation and set deterministic icon location on the shortcut. I also reinstalled your SendTo shortcut with your requested defaults: - `output-mode: same-dir` - `duplicate-mode: zid-dir` If you want to change behavior later, reinstall with different options, for example: - `python.\convert_media.py --install-sendto --output-mode converted-subdir --duplicate-mode skip`
